From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Quarrier <squarrier@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 08:33:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] glm5_next/cuda: admission at saturation, TF_GLM_MAX_QUEUED
 (MiaAI-Lab recipe patch 0082)

With every lane busy, a new request waited in an invisible queue for as long as the running ones took, with nothing
to tell its client to come back later. MiaAI-Lab's recipe v1.8 adds admission at saturation with patch
0082-tfcap-admission-cap (by johnwhited, after vLLM v1's check_admission): TF_GLM_MAX_QUEUED unset queues as every
scheduler always has (the recipe's default: its scripts/config.sh exports it empty); a number N refuses a foreground
request past the lanes plus N waiting ones at once with a CapacityError (patch 0081 renders it as 429 with
Retry-After: 5), while background requests bypass the cap and queue. On the AFD split the scheduler is the attention
node's (GlmScheduler, rank 0 of world 1). This ports it under the recipe's own switch name; unset is the default here
too:

- cuda/scheduler.py: Waiting.foreground_count, Scheduler's max_in_system and _check_admission, its call in submit,
  verbatim; foreground_count also skips TensorFold v0.6.5's close() stop entry (a None item), which the recipe's
  v0.6.0 queue never holds; the CapacityError import sits with the absolute imports (ruff's import order).
- multi.py: GlmScheduler reads TF_GLM_MAX_QUEUED into max_in_system (lanes + N) and submit runs the check first,
  before this tree's TF_GLM_QUEUED_CANCEL branch, as the patch runs it first in 0073's submit; the patch's unused
  CapacityError import in multi.py is left out (ruff).
- engine.py: a startup line naming the cap when TF_GLM_MAX_QUEUED is set.
- tests/test_glm_queued_cancel.py: the recipe's 0073 checks build their GlmScheduler without __init__, so the harness
  now also sets max_in_system = None (TF_GLM_MAX_QUEUED unset), as it sets queued_cancel. The recipe's own
  tools/test_queued_cancellation.py, unchanged since v1.6, stops at its first check on the recipe's v1.8 tree for this
  reason (AttributeError in the caller thread: "caller/scheduler did not make bounded progress"); at v1.7.1 it passes
  21/21.
- THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md: "Admission at saturation".

Unset (or empty), max_in_system is None and _check_admission returns at once: every request queues as before.

Tests (CPU): tests/test_glm_admission_cap.py (16, with TF_GLM_QUEUED_CANCEL unset and set): the cap is the lanes plus
TF_GLM_MAX_QUEUED (unset and empty: none); unset, a request past two busy lanes waits and is served; 0, it is refused
at once with no token sent, a background request still queues, and the busy replies finish; 1, one waits and the next
is refused, and a request after the lanes free is served; foreground_count skips background requests and the stop
entry; the base Scheduler never refuses without a cap.

