+## Admission at saturation (TF_GLM_MAX_QUEUED)
+
+`cuda/scheduler.py`'s `Scheduler._check_admission`, `Scheduler`'s `max_in_system` and `Waiting.foreground_count`, and
+`families/glm5_next/cuda/multi.py`'s `GlmScheduler` reading `TF_GLM_MAX_QUEUED` (unset, a request past the lanes
+queues as every scheduler always has; a number N, a foreground request past the lanes plus N waiting ones is refused at
+once with a `CapacityError`, while background requests still queue) are MiaAI-Lab's
+[GLM-5.3-Flash EXL3 2x DGX Spark recipe](https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold/tree/33b50fde06fd7ea604cbc6a663880068ab1e2ee4)
+patch 0082-tfcap-admission-cap (v1.8), written by [johnwhited](https://github.com/johnwhited) in
+[pull request #48](https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold/pull/48) (commit
+[`9d2fd5e`](https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold/commit/9d2fd5e32e2f9cf83a05f51a08ca4f440d9cf6f9))
+and applied by MiaAI-Lab as contributed; the recipe credits [vLLM](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm) v1's
+`check_admission` (Apache 2.0) as its reference. Under the recipe's Apache License 2.0 (see
+[the license text](LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt)). The switch is the recipe's own (`TF_GLM_MAX_QUEUED`, unset by default in
+its `scripts/config.sh`). Changes in the port: `Waiting.foreground_count` skips TensorFold v0.6.5's `close()` stop
+entry, which the recipe's queue never holds; the patch's unused `CapacityError` import in `multi.py` is left out;
+`GlmScheduler.submit` runs the check before this tree's `TF_GLM_QUEUED_CANCEL` branch; a startup line names the cap.
